.TH PAPERLIKE 1 "2026-11" "paperlike 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paperlike \- paper-like texture overlay for X11 desktops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paperlike
.RI [ command " [" args ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paperlike
lays a subtle paper or fabric texture over every monitor to soften glare and
harsh contrast, without tinting colours.
It runs as a small daemon with a tray icon, a control center popup and a
settings window.
.PP
Run without arguments,
.B paperlike
starts the daemon, or opens the control center if a daemon is already
running.
Any other command is sent to the running daemon over a Unix socket and its
reply is printed.
.PP
A compositing manager such as
.BR picom (1)
must be running; without one the overlay stays hidden.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Start the daemon in the foreground. Fails if one is already running.
.TP
.BR toggle " | " on " | " off
Switch the texture.
.TP
.B panel
Toggle the control center.
.TP
.BR settings " [\fIpage\fR]"
Open the settings window, optionally on
.IR page :
.BR general ", " texture ", " lamp ", " schedule ", " exceptions ", "
.BR display ", " hotkeys " or " about .
.TP
.BR next " | " prev
Switch to the next or previous texture.
.TP
.BR texture " \fIname\fR [" light | dark ]
Choose a texture for light or dark screens (default: whichever is showing).
Textures:
.BR matte ", " crosshatch ", " parchment ", " linen ", " cold-press ", "
.BR rice-paper ", " frost ", " felt ", " graphite ", " coarse-matte .
.TP
.BR intensity " \fIN\fR | +\fIN\fR | \-\fIN\fR"
Set or nudge the intensity of the current texture, in percent.
Each texture has its own range.
.TP
.BR lamp " [" on | off | toggle | \fIpreset\fR]
Control the Desk Lamp. Presets:
.BR candle ", " late-night ", " side-lamp ", " spotlight ", " sunset ", " ambient .
.TP
.BR snooze " \fIminutes\fR | " off
Hide the texture for a while, or bring it back early.
.TP
.BR theme " " light | dark | system | screen | sun
Choose how the light or dark texture is picked:
always light, always dark, following the GTK colour scheme, following what
each monitor shows, or by sunrise and sunset.
.TP
.BR status " [" \-\-json ]
Print the current state, for example for a status bar.
.TP
.B reload
Re-read the configuration file. Not normally needed, since edits apply
automatically.
.TP
.B quit
Stop the daemon.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of commands.
.TP
.BR version ", " \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH MOUSE
Clicking the tray icon opens the control center, right-clicking opens a menu,
middle-clicking toggles the texture and scrolling changes the intensity.
.SH HOTKEYS
Defaults, all configurable in the settings window:
.TP
.B Super+Alt+P
Toggle the texture.
.TP
.B Super+Alt+T
Next texture.
.TP
.B Super+Alt+O
Toggle the Desk Lamp.
.TP
.B Super+Alt+\e
Snooze for five minutes.
.TP
.BR Super+Alt+] " / " Super+Alt+[
Intensity up or down.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/paperlike/paperlike.toml
Settings. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/paperlike/paperlike.toml .
The daemon saves it when settings change, and applies edits made to it as
soon as the file is saved.
A file with errors is ignored until it parses again.
An older
.I config.toml
in the same directory is renamed on first start.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/paperlike<display>.sock
Command socket of the daemon for that display.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/paperlike.desktop
Created by the \(lqOpen at login\(rq setting.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
The X display to cover.
.TP
.B PAPERLIKE_DEBUG
If set, X protocol errors are logged to standard error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 for an invalid command, and 3 for
.B status
when no daemon is running.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start with i3, in
.IR ~/.config/i3/config :
.PP
.RS
.nf
exec \-\-no\-startup\-id paperlike
bindsym $mod+Mod1+t exec \-\-no\-startup\-id paperlike next
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR picom (1),
.BR i3 (1)
